        "mission_intent": "Team, in light of the upcoming quarterly close, I need you to perform a comprehensive evaluation of all identified control deficiencies across our financial reporting processes and classify each as a significant deficiency or material weakness, applying the framework from AS 2201. Specifically, I want the assessment to consider the magnitude of potential misstatements \u2014 keeping in mind that overstatements are generally bounded by recorded amounts while understatements can exceed them \u2014 and to evaluate whether any compensating controls operate at a sufficient level of precision to mitigate the risk. The analysis should also flag any indicators of material weakness, such as prior restatements, any fraud involvement by senior management, or instances where our auditors identified material misstatements that our controls failed to catch. Here's where I need your best judgment: I want the final deliverable to represent the \"best possible\" classification of every deficiency, but I don't want you to set any bright-line quantitative materiality threshold \u2014 just use professional judgment to ensure nothing material slips through. Please have this completed and ready for the audit committee package by end of day Friday, even though the complete population of Q3 control testing results won't be available from the outsourced testing team until the following Monday. Coordinate with the external auditors as needed and document your rationale for each classification in the deficiency tracker in Workiva.",
